                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Either: Henry Sampson Woodfall,  printer and editor of the <title>Public Advertiser</title>
   or William Woodfall (1745-1803), his brother, who was printer of the <title>Morning Chrionicle</title> until his death in 1803.</p>
                        <p>Entries to Woodfall after 1805 (H S Woodfall's death) (there are 9 in 1823) are assumed to be to <persName key="WOO06">George Woodfall </persName>
    (1767-1844) who was the son of  Henry Sampson Woodfall, and nephew of William and was also a newspaper editor and printer.</p>
